# ACPI firmware-data regression (tests/headless, acpi-firmware-data; the
# kernel's Firmware_Data_Tag roots, devmgr's Data_Window_Request): stands in
# for acpi-backend.svc's launch approved for acpi-firmware-data beside
# acpi-hardware and acpi-pci-config (which lets it find a PCI BAR to ask
# for). The approved entry gets devmgr's firmware-data endpoint
# ("hardware-data"); the same image started as acpi-data-unapproved.app does
# not, and is refused through the ordinary "device-manager" endpoint.
# "tables" is the firmware snapshot reader, so the program finds the FACS
# and the MCFG itself.
(Executable_Manifest
  identity => "com.cubit.acpi-data-check"
  version => "0.1.0"
  requests => [
    (Request.Firmware_Snapshot "tables")
    (Request.ACPI_Hardware "hardware")
    (service "device-manager" "device-manager")])
